GCP FOUNDATION AND HIERARCHY

Everything lives in hierarchy

Organization -> Folder -> Project -> Resources

Personal account may start directly with a project without an organization or folder.

Project are where you actually create and manage resources.

2.The project is the core boundary.

A project is where resources live and where access , APIs , billing and quotas are managed.

Project Name : Human-readable label , can be changed.
Project ID : Globally unique string , can not be changed.
Project Number : Auto-assigned numeric identifier.


A project contains/Manages.
IAM , APIs (Application programming Interface.) ,Billing ,VPC and more

3.Identity And Access Management .
IAM  answers one question: who are you and what can you do on which resource.

IAM POLICY = PRINCIPAL: who get access + ROLE: Bundle of permissions

Principal : An identity that receives access : user ,group ,service account ,workload identity
Ex: dev@gmail.com

Permission : One specific action like a view a resource , create a VM permission read a bucket you do not assign these directly.

ROLE : A collection of permissions you grant roles not individual permissions

IAM POLICY : Decides which principal gets which role at which resources level.

Ex : dev@gmail.com has the compute admin role on devops-project


4.Three types of roles

Basic Roles : Viewer , Editor , Owner , Very Broad . Avoid in production.
Predefined Roles : Compute Admin , Storage Admin , managed by Google , specific to a service
Custom Roles : Permissions you choose yourself when predefined roles are too broad or too narrow

5.IAM INHERITANCE : Access flows downward

A policy granted at a higher supported level is inherited by everything below it.
 
Architecture

The same thing applies from organization down to folder ,project and resources.

Grant access at the lowest level that works to keep it isolate.

6.Service Account : Identity for automation

A service account is used by application , workloads ,automation or CI/CD not by human.

GITHUB ACTIONS -> SERVICE ACCOUNT -> IAM -> GCP RESOURCES.
TERRAFORM -> terraform-sa -> i am permissions -> VPC/VM/STORAGE.


Critical for DevOps : Pipelines and tools should use service account not personal logins.
Give each service account only the roles its job needs.

7.AuthN : Prove who are you . , AUTHZ : Deciding what you are allowed to do . IAM handles this.

