GCP VPC 
VPC = Virtual Private Cloud a private isolated virtual network inside GCP where your VMs , resources connected and talk
each other.


VPC Network : Global resources
Subnet A : Regional Spans all zones in asia-south1
Subnet B : Regional Spans all zones in us-central1
Subnet C : Regional Spans all zones in europe-west1

Subnet : Regional IP ranges where resources get internal IPs
Routes : Decides where traffic is flow.
Firewall Rules : Decides which traffic is allowed or denied.
IP Addresses : Internal (private) and external (public).

A VPC belongs to a project , Resources in one VPC can reach other on internal IPs across regions
(if firewall allows).

2.Network Modes : Auto mode vs Custom Mode 
Auto Mode :
1. One subnet auto-created in every region
2. Uses predefined ranges from 10.128.0.0/9
3. New regions get subnets automatically
4. Best for testing

Custom Mode :
1.No subnets create automatically.
2.You choose regions and IP ranges.
3.Full control of IP Planning.
4.Recommonded for production.

Default network in a new project is an auto mode network .

Auto mode ranges are the same in every project so they can overlap with each other 
networks or on-premises . Auto mode can be converted to custom mode , but not back  

Internal IP :
Private IP from the subnet range .
Used for traffic inside the VPC.
Every VM has one.

External IP :
1.Public reachable from internet
2.Optional for a VM
3.External IPV4 addresses are billed.

EPHEMERAL IP :
1.Assigned automatically 
2.Can change when VM is stopped and started.
3.Fine for temporary workloads.

Static (Reserved) :
Reserved for your project.
Stays the same until you release it.
Use for DNS records or allow-list.

4.Routes
1.Default Route :System generated (0.0.0.0/0)
2.Subnet Route :System generated one per subnet range.
3.Subnet Route : Created by you for a specific range
4.Dynamic Route : BGP (Border Gateway protocol) mainly used for VPN

5.VPC Firewall Rules
Rules are defined at the VPC level and enforced on each VM they are stateful 
